{
  "_readme": [
    "Competitor-mapped public rate card (docs/pricing-rate-card.md). Apply after sign-off:",
    "1) POST /api/v1/admin/price-plan   with .plan  -> note the returned id",
    "2) For each .rules[]: set pricePlanId to that id, POST /api/v1/admin/price-plan/rule",
    "All prices USD/hour (platform base currency must be USD).",
    "GPU rules are additive on top of the CPU/RAM component rules — see the rate card's",
    "calibration note before changing values. gpu_model aliases follow the pci-alias form.",
    "kubernetes_cluster is the managed-k8s CONTROL-PLANE fee only, priced per CP replica",
    "(attrs: display_name/version/status/endpoint/cp_replicas/node_groups — see",
    "internal/cloud/billingresource/kubernetescluster.go). A cluster's worker VMs, volumes",
    "and API load balancer live in the customer's own keystone tenant and already bill via",
    "the existing instance/volume/load_balancer rules — never add k8s rules for them here",
    "(double-charge). Billing starts once the control-plane endpoint exists; the rate below",
    "is a placeholder until the plan-§6 CP-pricing decision (free CP vs paid HA vs flat fee).",
    "_pendingRules are NOT applied by the steps above. kubernetes_cluster sits there (matching the commented-out twin in price-plan-seed.sql) until the plan-§6 CP-pricing decision; move it into .rules to activate, and update the SQL twin in the same change.",
    "kubernetes_cluster: EKS-style flat control-plane fee via the generic `existence` attribute (0.10/h ~= $73/mo); worker VMs/volumes/LBs bill through the existing rules. bucket: object storage priced per stored GB-hour (size_gb, ceil'd), or swap attributeName to `existence` for a flat per-bucket fee.",
    "database_cluster is the managed-database FULL price (unlike kubernetes_cluster): the DB pods and volumes run on ops-owned nodes, so nothing else bills them. Attributes are pre-multiplied totals (vcpus_total/ram_gb_total/storage_gb_total = per-instance x replicas — see internal/cloud/billingresource/databasecluster.go). The endpoint gate DEFERS the charge while the Octavia VIP is absent and back-bills the current cycle's elapsed hours once it appears (the engine freezes the watermark at createdAt; it does not waive them). Keep in sync with the database_cluster entries in price-plan-seed.sql.",
    "database_cluster rates are DIGITALOCEAN-PARITY (managed-databases price list, read 2026-08-03; monthly/730h): PG+MySQL fit exactly at the small tiers with $2/vCPU-mo + $11/GB-RAM-mo + $0.215/GB-disk-mo -> 0.002740/0.015068/0.000295 per hour (mariadb=MySQL rates, ferretdb=Mongo rates which are within 1% of PG so PG rates reused); Valkey $2.15/$10.70/$0.215 -> 0.002945/0.014658/0.000295; OpenSearch $2/$4.50/$0.215 -> 0.002740/0.006164/0.000295 (exact on all three DO tiers); Kafka is RAM-rated only ($21/GB-RAM-mo + storage; DO prices the 3-broker cluster, vCPU does not move price across DO's two plans) -> 0.028767 ram + 0.000295 storage. One rule per engine (filter engine eq ...) because rule filters have no OR. Re-derive when DO reprices."
  ],
